WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.023 --> 00:00:03.400
- I think a lot of runners are discouraged

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.810
that shoes have become such
a huge focus in a sport

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:09.090
that used to be seen as so elemental,

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:11.810
it was just about your
training, and your fitness,

00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:13.700
and you on the open road,

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:16.740
and this shoe technology
controversy has changed all that.

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:19.520
People wonder where was
this regulation earlier?

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:23.240
They feel like, not all brands
were given the same chance

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:25.030
to develop this technology,

00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:26.890
that may be the spirit of the rules

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:29.700
was largely ignored for several years.

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:30.950
- [Narrator] On January 31st,

00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:34.020
World Athletics Track and
Field's World Governing Body

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:36.420
release new regulations about shoes worn

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:38.400
in elite marathon competition,

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.430
in the wake of record breaking times

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:43.270
from runners wearing Nike Vaporfly shoes.

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:45.360
The regulations set specific limits

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:48.390
about the height and composition
of distance running shoes.

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:50.710
Soles can be no thicker
than 40 millimeters,

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:54.180
and any rigid plates must
be in one continuous plane.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:56.690
2020 is an Olympic year,

00:00:56.690 --> 00:00:59.510
the January ruling means
athletes can wear prototypes

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:01.340
in February's Olympic trials,

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:04.870
but any new shoes must be
available at retail by April 30th

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:07.440
if they are to be worn
at the Tokyo Olympics.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:09.830
So, how are shoe companies scrambling

00:01:09.830 --> 00:01:12.650
to match Nike's Vaporfly technology?

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:15.260
- Well, I think the first
objection by critics

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:16.340
was the timing.

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:19.540
Because, World Athletics
had received complaints

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:22.840
about these Nike shoes
or concerns at least

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:25.620
for at least the past two or three years.

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:27.420
And yet, it took until January

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:30.550
for them to take any
really specific action.

00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:32.677
So, I think competing brands were saying,

00:01:32.677 --> 00:01:34.957
"Hey, this is an Olympic year.

00:01:34.957 --> 00:01:37.267
"This is incredibly important
for not only the development

00:01:37.267 --> 00:01:39.507
"of our technology but
also for our competitors

00:01:39.507 --> 00:01:42.310
"who have their highest
profile competition."

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:44.320
The U.S. is almost unique in the world

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:48.010
in that it holds trials for
the Olympic marathon team.

00:01:48.010 --> 00:01:50.480
Most other nations hand
select their marathoners,

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:52.240
but in the case of the U.S.,

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:54.640
you have to finish in the
top three among women or men

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:55.850
to qualify.

00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:57.880
Of course, that makes
it incredibly important

00:01:57.880 --> 00:02:00.200
that you're in shape,
and that you have a shoe

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:02.310
that can beat other runners.

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:03.210
- [Narrator] Earlier this year,

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:05.510
the Wall Street Journal
studied the Vaporfly,

00:02:05.510 --> 00:02:07.370
asking experts to dissect the shoe

00:02:07.370 --> 00:02:09.940
to demonstrate what some
athletes and critics

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:12.290
say give the shoes an advantage.

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:15.019
- Second, you can see the full
length carbon fiber plate.

00:02:15.019 --> 00:02:19.430
And this carbon fiber plate
adds a lot of stiffness

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:21.720
and stability to the shoe as well.

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:23.280
- [Narrator] It's a
race to spring deadline

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:25.850
for brands to release shoes
if they haven't already,

00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:27.450
that contain a carbon plate

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:31.030
and comply with the new
World Athletics regulations.

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:33.070
While Hoka One own a shoe comparable

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:34.460
to the Vaporfly technology,

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:36.700
and has been out since May 2019,

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:39.000
we'll see debuts from brands like Saucony,

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:41.830
with their Endorphin Pro,
which will be released globally

00:02:41.830 --> 00:02:43.330
on April 15.

00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:45.610
Brooks will publicly launched
their Hyperion Elite shoe

00:02:45.610 --> 00:02:46.770
on February 29th,

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:49.150
but announced five days
before the Olympic trials

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:51.310
that some of their elite
athletes will be racing

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:54.200
in the next iteration,
the Hyperion elite two,

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:55.900
which will hit the market in late April,

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:58.220
ahead of the April 30th deadline.

00:02:58.220 --> 00:03:00.790
Adidas Adizero Pro will
be available to the public

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:04.590
in select markets from April
1 and worldwide by May 15.

00:03:04.590 --> 00:03:07.407
New Balance released their
FuelCell TC in February,

00:03:07.407 --> 00:03:10.770
and ASICS will release their
Metaracer shoe in spring,

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:13.340
but Nike's athletes may
wear the new Alphafly

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:14.810
on February, 29th.

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:17.140
It does have a thicker
sole than the Vaporfly,

00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:18.980
but the brand has said it will comply

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:20.560
with the new regulations.

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:22.350
- Privately, and
especially to one another,

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:25.320
some runners who run on competing shoes,

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:28.440
have expressed concern about
whether theirs will match up,

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:29.350
not only with the current Nikes,

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:33.840
but these yet unseen new Nikes.

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:36.290
I think some athletes
and brands feel that Nike

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:38.040
has too much influence in the sport.

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:42.080
It's the leading brand in
performance running shoes,

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:44.510
and sponsors many, many athletes,

00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:46.440
sponsors U.S.A. track and field.

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:48.250
The president of World Athletics

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:50.620
is a longtime former
Nike sponsored athlete.

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:53.570
Competitors worry that
maybe that relationship

00:03:53.570 --> 00:03:56.010
is a little bit too close with the body

00:03:56.010 --> 00:03:58.240
that's supposed to be regulating it.

00:03:58.240 --> 00:03:59.970
- [Narrator] When asked
about the body's independence

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:02.717
from Nike, World Athletics
responded in a statement,

00:04:02.717 --> 00:04:04.927
"We need to balance what
is currently in the market

00:04:04.927 --> 00:04:06.217
"at an elite level

00:04:06.217 --> 00:04:08.457
"and draw a line by prohibiting shoes

00:04:08.457 --> 00:04:11.027
"that may go further than what
is currently on the market,

00:04:11.027 --> 00:04:13.320
"until further research is undertaken."

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:15.747
And that, "No shoe company
was directly involved

00:04:15.747 --> 00:04:17.540
"in shaping the regulations."

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:19.360
A Nike spokesperson said in a statement

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:20.327
to the Wall Street Journal,

00:04:20.327 --> 00:04:22.387
"We believe the New World athletics rules

00:04:22.387 --> 00:04:24.687
"will stifle innovation
over the long term,

00:04:24.687 --> 00:04:28.680
"ultimately impacting
athletes, consumers, and fans".

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:31.187
Brooks said in a comment
to the Wall Street Journal,

00:04:31.187 --> 00:04:34.057
"Generally we would spend
more time between prototype

00:04:34.057 --> 00:04:35.727
"and bringing a shoe to market,

00:04:35.727 --> 00:04:37.667
"but the recent WA ruling pushed us

00:04:37.667 --> 00:04:40.270
"to reassess our go-to-market strategy."

00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:43.270
- One of the reasons why
these questions about shoes

00:04:43.270 --> 00:04:44.180
are so important

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:46.470
is because running isn't only for elites.

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:49.240
Last year in the U.S.,
about 15 million people

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:50.960
went running at least once.

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:53.100
And if there's a shoe that someone thinks

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:56.510
is gonna make them run a half
marathon or a 10k faster,

00:04:56.510 --> 00:04:58.370
they might be very
interested in buying it.

00:04:58.370 --> 00:05:01.680
So, this is not only
a question for elites,

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:03.923
but it's also a question for the market.

